    <h2>How it is stored in our database</h2>
    <p>Loaded by <code>db/changelog/seed/05-redemptions.yaml</code> into two tables. Parts A, B and C share one table
        because they have the same grain: one row per vendor county and period.</p>

    <h3><code>redemption_by_family</code></h3>
    <p>12,063 rows: Parts A, B and C combined.</p>
    <table>
        <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Published column</th>
        </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>id</code></td>
            <td>bigint</td>
            <td>Generated key.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>part</code></td>
            <td>varchar(1)</td>
            <td>The source file: <code>A</code>, <code>B</code> or <code>C</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>vendor_county_code</code></td>
            <td>smallint</td>
            <td>Vendor County Code. <code>0</code> is Statewide.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>vendor_county</code></td>
            <td>varchar(50)</td>
            <td>Vendor County</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>year</code></td>
            <td>smallint</td>
            <td rowspan="2">Obligation Year and Month. <code>2019</code> is an annual row (<code>month</code> is <code>NULL</code>);
                <code>201901</code> is January 2019.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>month</code></td>
            <td>smallint</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>families_redeemed</code></td>
            <td>integer</td>
            <td>Number of Families Redeemed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>food_instruments_redeemed</code></td>
            <td>integer</td>
            <td>Number of Food Instruments Redeemed (parts A and B)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>food_instrument_dollars</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Dollar Amount of Food Instruments (parts A and B)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>ebt_transactions</code></td>
            <td>integer</td>
            <td>Number of EBT Transactions (parts B and C)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>ebt_dollars</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Dollar Amount of EBT Transactions (parts B and C)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>average_cost_per_family</code></td>
            <td>numeric(12,2)</td>
            <td>Average Cost per Family</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>statewide_infant_formula_rebate</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Statewide Infant Formula Rebate. Statewide rows only.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>total_cost_adjusted</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Total Cost Adjusted. Statewide rows only.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>average_cost_adjusted</code></td>
            <td>numeric(12,2)</td>
            <td>Average Cost Adjusted. Statewide rows only.</td>
        </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3><code>redemption_by_participant_category</code></h3>
    <p>33,851 rows, 2010 to 2018.</p>
    <table>
        <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Published column</th>
        </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>id</code></td>
            <td>bigint</td>
            <td>Generated key.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>vendor_county</code></td>
            <td>varchar(50)</td>
            <td>Vendor Location. Published in capitals; stored in title case (<code>SAN LUIS OBISPO</code> becomes
                <code>San Luis Obispo</code>) to match the other tables. <code>STATEWIDE</code> and <code>STATEWIDE
                    ANNUAL</code> both become <code>Statewide</code>.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>participant_category</code></td>
            <td>varchar(50)</td>
            <td>Participant Category: Breastfeeding Mother, Child, Infant, Non-Breastfeeding Mother or Prenatal. <code>ALL</code>,
                used on the statewide annual totals, becomes <code>All</code>.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>year</code></td>
            <td>smallint</td>
            <td rowspan="2">Year Month. <code>2010</code> is an annual row; <code>2010-01</code> is January 2010.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>month</code></td>
            <td>smallint</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>participants_redeemed</code></td>
            <td>integer</td>
            <td>Number of Participants Redeemed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>vouchers_redeemed</code></td>
            <td>integer</td>
            <td>Number Vouchers Redeemed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>total_cost</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Total Cost Vouchers</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>average_cost</code></td>
            <td>numeric(12,2)</td>
            <td>Average Cost</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>statewide_infant_formula_rebate</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Statewide Infant Formula Rebate</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>total_cost_adjusted</code></td>
            <td>numeric(15,2)</td>
            <td>Total Cost Vouchers Adjusted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>average_cost_adjusted</code></td>
            <td>numeric(12,2)</td>
            <td>Average Cost Adjusted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>state_average_cost_adjusted</code></td>
            <td>numeric(12,2)</td>
            <td>State Average Cost Adjusted</td>
        </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Notes</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>The description says suppressed cells are marked “–”. The family count files actually use <code>-</code> and
            the participant category file uses <code>*</code>. All of them are stored as <code>NULL</code>.
        </li>
        <li>Columns that do not apply to a part are also <code>NULL</code>: no EBT values in part A and no food
            instrument values in part C. In part B, food instruments stop and EBT starts partway through.
        </li>
        <li>Annual rows sit next to monthly rows. Filter on <code>month IS NULL</code> for annual totals, or <code>month
            IS NOT NULL</code> to sum months yourself.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>API</h2>
    <table>
        <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Request</th>
            <th>Returns</th>
        </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>GET /api/redemptions/by-family</code></td>
            <td>Pages of <code>redemption_by_family</code> rows.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>GET /api/redemptions/by-participant-category</code></td>
            <td>Pages of <code>redemption_by_participant_category</code> rows. Also takes <code>category</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Both take <code>county</code>, <code>year</code>, <code>month</code>, <code>annual</code> (<code>true</code> for
        annual rows only, <code>false</code> for monthly rows only), <code>page</code> and <code>size</code> (up to
        1,000). For example, the statewide annual totals:</p>
    <pre><code>GET /api/redemptions/by-family?county=Statewide&amp;annual=true</code></pre>
    <p>The same query in SQL:</p>
    <pre><code>SELECT year, part, families_redeemed, food_instrument_dollars, ebt_dollars
FROM redemption_by_family
WHERE vendor_county = 'Statewide' AND month IS NULL
ORDER BY year;</code></pre>
{% endblock %}
